<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A stretch has stretch factor <m>{2}</m> and the x-axis invariant.</p><p>(a) Write down its matrix.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the image of the point <m>({-3},\,{4})</m>.</p><div>( <fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="5" name="ans3"/> )   </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Every point off the invariant axis moves at right angles to it, and its distance from that axis is multiplied by the stretch factor. With the x-axis invariant, points on the x-axis do not move and the y-coordinate is multiplied by <m>{2}</m>.</p><p>(a) The images of (1, 0) and (0, 1) are the columns: <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{c} -3 \\ 4 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{c} -3 \\ 8 \end{array}\right]}</m>, so the image is <m>({-3},\,{8})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-3</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>8</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>